# Testing and quality

Follow `docs/engineering/testing-quality-gates.md`.

- Test observable behavior with positive, negative, boundary, authorization,
  failure, expiry, and retry cases as applicable.
- Keep tests deterministic, isolated, order-independent, and explicit about
  UTC time.
- Do not add assertion-free coverage tests.
- Do not disable or weaken a test to bypass a defect, compilation problem,
  stubbing issue, visibility issue, or flakiness.
- Parameterize data-only variations; keep distinct behaviors separate.
- Verify coverage from generated reports rather than estimating it.
- Required thresholds are 80% overall coverage, 90% new-code coverage, no new
  blocker/critical Sonar findings, and no more than 3% duplication.
- Generated/configuration exclusions require documented review.
- Report test commands, results, coverage, limitations, and applicable
  security/accessibility/performance/recovery evidence.
